[Unity Development Rules]
1. DO NOT truncate code with comments like "// keep existing code". Always output the full class or method being modified.
2. Maintain all [SerializeField] fields and Unity callback methods unless explicitly asked to remove them.
3. After writing code, provide a brief "Verification Checklist" showing how this code meets the user's requirements.
4. The user's saved Unity scene is the source of truth. Do not edit .unity scene files, do not run TestRoomSetup auto-apply, and do not use Unity MCP to change the scene unless the user explicitly asks to modify the scene.
